{"causes": ["Angel Grimoard's birth into the influential Grimoard noble family provided him with significant social and political advantages within 14th-century France.", "His younger brother, Guillaume de Grimoard, being elected Pope Urban V in 1362 directly propelled Angel's ecclesiastical career to the highest echelons of the Church.", "The ongoing political instability and the Great Schism within the Catholic Church created a demand for skilled administrators and diplomats like Grimoard to manage papal affairs."], "effects": ["Angel Grimoard's rise as a cardinal strengthened the administrative and diplomatic capacity of the Avignon Papacy during a period of significant challenge.", "His influential position allowed him to support and solidify the Avignon line of popes, thereby deepening and prolonging the Western Schism.", "Grimoard's legatine missions across Europe helped to enforce papal authority and mediate regional conflicts, even as the Church itself was divided."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "pope-urban-v", "sourceName": "Pope Urban V", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "angel-grimoard", "targetName": "Angel Grimoard", "context": "Pope Urban V's election in 1362 directly influenced and accelerated his brother Angel Grimoard's ecclesiastical career."}, {"sourceSlug": "angel-grimoard", "sourceName": "Angel Grimoard", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "western-schism", "targetName": "Western Schism", "context": "Angel Grimoard participated in the Western Schism by supporting the Avignon papacy after 1378, contributing to the Church's division."}, {"sourceSlug": "angel-grimoard", "sourceName": "Angel Grimoard", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "avignon-france", "targetName": "Avignon, France", "context": "Angel Grimoard's career as Bishop and Cardinal was primarily centered in Avignon, France, the seat of the papacy for much of his life."}, {"sourceSlug": "angel-grimoard", "sourceName": "Angel Grimoard", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "pope-gregory-xi", "targetName": "Pope Gregory XI", "context": "Angel Grimoard collaborated with Pope Gregory XI as a cardinal and legate, supporting his administration and the return of the papacy to Rome in 1377."}, {"sourceSlug": "angel-grimoard", "sourceName": "Angel Grimoard", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "roman-curia", "targetName": "Roman Curia", "context": "As a Cardinal-Bishop, Angel Grimoard exerted significant influence on the administrative and diplomatic functions of the Roman Curia during the Avignon Papacy."}], "places": [{"name": "Avignon, France", "role": "Major See and Residence"}, {"name": "Rome, Italy", "role": "Cardinalate See"}, {"name": "Grisac, France", "role": "Familial Origin"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Angel Grimoard", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "angel-grimoard"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1528423", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_de_Grimoard"], "tags": ["France", "Religious Figures", "Europe", "comparative-religion", "doctrine-development", "cultural-diffusion"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Angel Grimoard was a pivotal figure in the Avignon Papacy and the early Western Schism, whose administrative and diplomatic actions, particularly his support for the Avignon line, directly contributed to the decades-long division of the Catholic Church.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:20:32Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#37442013350", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Angel de Grimoard, also recorded as Angelic or Anglic, was a French canon regular and a Cardinal. He was the younger brother of Pope Urban V.", "newValue": "Angel de Grimoard (d. 1388), a distinguished French canon regular, rose to prominence as a Cardinal during a tumultuous period for the Catholic Church, marked by the Avignon Papacy and the nascent Western Schism. His ecclesiastical career was significantly shaped by his familial connection to Pope Urban V, his younger brother, whose papacy elevated him to positions of immense influence. Grimoard served as a key administrative and diplomatic figure within the papal curia, wielding authority across Western Europe and playing a crucial, albeit complex, role in attempts to navigate the deep divisions that afflicted Christendom.

Beginning his career as an Augustinian canon, Grimoard's ascent was rapid following his brother's election to the papacy in 1362. He was swiftly appointed Bishop of Avignon in 1362, then elevated to Cardinal-Priest of San Pietro in Vincoli in 1366, and finally Cardinal-Bishop of Albano in 1367. Throughout these appointments, he acted as a papal legate on numerous critical missions, notably to Italy and Spain, where he worked to secure allegiances, mediate disputes, and enforce papal authority. His administrative acumen was vital in managing the complex finances and political relationships of the Avignon Curia, particularly in the lead-up to Pope Gregory XI's return to Rome.

Grimoard's legacy is intertwined with the deepening crisis of the Western Schism. After Gregory XI's death and the contentious election of Urban VI in Rome, Grimoard initially supported the Avignon claimant, Clement VII, recognizing him due to his familial ties and the perceived illegitimacy of the Roman election by some cardinals. His continued support for the Avignon line solidified the schism's institutional framework, contributing to the decades-long division that would plague the Church. His efforts, though ultimately divisive, underscore the profound challenges faced by church leaders attempting to maintain unity amidst conflicting claims to papal legitimacy."}, {"timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:20:32Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#37442013350", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1320, Le Pont-de-Montvert"}, {"title": "Spiritual seeking and religious community formation", "type": "Idea", "year": "1320, Le Pont-de-Montvert"}], "newValue": ["Angel Grimoard's birth into the influential Grimoard noble family provided him with significant social and political advantages within 14th-century France.", "His younger brother, Guillaume de Grimoard, being elected Pope Urban V in 1362 directly propelled Angel's ecclesiastical career to the highest echelons of the Church.", "The ongoing political instability and the Great Schism within the Catholic Church created a demand for skilled administrators and diplomats like Grimoard to manage papal affairs."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:20:32Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#37442013350", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped religious practice and spiritual communities", "type": "Idea", "year": "1388-04-22"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "yea